{
  "_note": "Delivery SLA / turnaround rules for Laundry Khalas (task spec §§23-25). DB-driven: scripts/seed_delivery_sla.py imports this into the `delivery_sla_rules` table (runtime source of truth); services/delivery.py reads the DB (JSON fallback) and computes each item's turnaround, Express eligibility and the order-level delivery estimate. Rules are matched most-specific-first: an item-level rule (item_codes) overrides its category default. `day_type` is CALENDAR by default (see meta.day_type) — whether 'days' means calendar or working days is a BUSINESS DECISION kept configurable here, NOT buried in the LLM prompt. Express = 12h, eligible ONLY for Wash & Fold / Clean & Press / Press Only; the Express surcharge is intentionally NULL (not invented — the business must configure express_surcharge_aed before it is charged).",
